  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sudan ACJR 2024 (Joint Budget)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SUMMARY
The Sudan Joint Response 2024, responding to the needs that have arisen in the famine-like conditions, will be implemented through a consortium led by Plan International and consisting of 1) FPDO (Plan International), 2) Child Development Foundation (Save the Children), 3) SUDO (CARE), 4) World Relief and 5) HOPE (Tearfund), 6) Alsawaid Alkhadara Organization (World Vision), 7) SOS Sahel and 8) GFO (ZOA). The joint budget is allocated by the Sudan Joint Response partners. The joint budget is set aside to facilitate regional meetings, joint activities, travel and communication costs, and real time review. The budget is managed by Plan International in its role as JR lead.</narrative>
  </description>
